  "id": "representative-design",
  "term": "representative design",
  "definition": "Representative design is an approach to experiment design used to improve external validity by making the research situation more like the real-world setting in which decisions or behavior normally occur. In this context, it means studying people under conditions that better reflect the live environment rather than relying only on artificial laboratory tasks.",
